{
 "slug": "test/peaks",
 "about": "Peak finding, near-duplicate removal, spectrum averaging, guitar auto-selection and the full-set save, on TapToneAnalyzer. The union of the three editions' cases; the expected values are Swift's (its production code, run by a minting test), in 32-bit Float — numbers are compared at 'tolerance': |actual - expected| <= relative * |expected| + absolute; strings and counts exactly. 'findPeaks': a spectrum — 'gaussians' (each peak 'peakDB' + -(f - peakHz)^2 / (2 sigma^2), sigma = halfWidthHz / 2.355, floored at noiseFloor, the element-wise maximum of the peaks; bins at i * (sampleRate / 2) / (binCount - 1)), 'flat' (one value; bins binSpacingHz apart, or as for gaussians), or 'triangle' (peakDB - slopeDBPerBin * |i - peakBin|, bins binSpacingHz apart) — with the analyzer's peakMinThreshold, minFrequency, maxFrequency and an optional peakMinOverride → every peak returned, in order (frequency, magnitude, quality, bandwidth, pitchNote, pitchCents, pitchFrequency). 'removeDuplicatePeaks': peaks in → the indices of those kept, in order. 'averageSpectra': taps → the averaged magnitudes and frequencies. 'autoSelection': a findPeaks case's peaks under a guitar type → each peak's mode (classifyAll) and the indices guitarModeSelectedPeakIDs selects. 'fullSetSave': a fixture's spectrum, frozen, its full set found at the -100 dB floor, Peak Min applied → the displayed and saved counts, whether the Air peak (within 1 Hz of airHz) is in each, whether every displayed peak is saved, whether every saved peak has its own id; then the durable set replaced by its first 'loadedFirst' peaks, as a loaded measurement's → that set is saved as it is. 'from' notes which editions' tests a case came from.",
 "tolerance": {
  "relative": 1e-05,
  "absolute": 0.0001
 },
